{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean","id":532418,"title":"Some thoughts on the \"Humanism vs Transhumanism\" debate in Promethean.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-29T15:42:53-07:00","id":532418,"title":"Some thoughts on the \"Humanism vs Transhumanism\" debate in Promethean.","content":"I recently read the comments on some blog updates for the Promethean 2ed and this was the first I learned that &quot;humanism vs transhumanism&quot; seems to have been a major, long-term debate concerning the Promethean game. This really caught my interest, as it's similarly been a big issue for my group. I actually made an account just because I was so interested in hearing different perspectives on this issue. I'll start by saying that I've always really enjoyed when the games offer multiple &quot;alternative&quot; truths and possible paths, rather than assuming things must be one way, but when they don't my group has never hesitated to alter things to fit our preferred narrative. I appreciate that the ability to do this is stressed in the blog posts, as well. We did, in fact, largely verge from the intended path of the series and, in doing so, I think it was one of the games we've most enjoyed playing. This fact makes me sad to see a lot of people saying Promethean is &quot;unplayable&quot; due to the &quot;philosophical content&quot;, because I think it's a great concept that can easily be tweeked to fit multiple perspectives without a monumental effort.<br /> <br /> I never actually saw the complaint my group had with the Pilgrimage as one of a preference for transhumanism. To me, transhumanistic themes are more in-line with some Mage, Hunter and general God-Machine aspects. There are Legacies in the Mage material that certainly address transhumanism and, personally, I've always approached the Free Council as having a strong transhumanist slant among their majority. Some of the Hunter groups, like the Cheiron Group, Utopia Now or The Knights of Adrian certainly have strong transhumanist elements, but I feel like Hunter is especially thick with this philosophy. When it comes to Promethean, I would have only really even thought &quot;transhumanism&quot; when it came to certain technologically heavy backgrounds for the Unfleshed. Even then, though, the person created isn't and was never human. <br /> <br /> The fact that they weren't human and, yet, their only acceptable goal is to become so is what was unappealing to my group. Of course there are drawbacks of being a Promethean, extreme ones. The Wasteland is the one that can't really be ignored simply by removing themselves from human society, but a big focus on what's &quot;wrong&quot; with being a Promethean is that humans react negatively to them. The general feelings of my group were probably colored largely by the fact that we're all somewhere on the LGBT spectrum and some have alternative gender identities they've struggled with, as well as some of those same people experiencing the double edged bigotry sword of added racism, so a couple of our group members couldn't get past the idea that becoming human was just giving up what made the Promethean who they were in order to gain acceptance from their tormenters. There was no way they could get comfortable with the idea of a character that would sacrifice their inherent individuality (as the players saw it, at least) in order to appeal to the majority expectations. It would always come back as a reflection of the question in their mind, &quot;If there was a way to undo the thing people persecute ME for, should I take that choice?&quot;. A game that in any way implied they should caused them discomfort and ruined their interest.<br /> <br /> However, we could recognize that this wasn't really the intended message. The Prometheans aren't facing homophobia or racism, even if the rejection they experience can pick at the insecurities of players that have experienced those things. We didn't feel the need to shun the material, because it actually had a lot of aspects that really hit home with us. The journey of these beings to overcome the external torments inflicted on them and find peace inside themselves was actually extremely appealing to us without the suggested endgame goal. Our alternative was that the endgame goal wouldn't be to become human, but to find a way to control the Divine Fire inside ourselves so that our characters wouldn't have to give up what they were, their memories, etc, and could continue on with their lives gaining acceptance for what they were and not only by sacrificing themselves to become something new.<br /> <br /> We focused our character Refinements on Mercurius, Stannum, Argentum, Cobalus and Plumbum. We made it a focus to study Pyros, but also the existence of other supernatural creatures, but not to see how it was lesser or more flawed than the existence of humans. We found an interesting theme to explore in our game was how supernatural entities and mortal humans were truly no better or worse than each other. &quot;Humanity&quot; wasn't just for humans. A werewolf, or vampire or even more &quot;non-human&quot; creatures could be kind, helpful beings that used their power to help others. We, as Promethean, could do that. Some mortal human Hunter archetypes claim to be doing good by slaughtering supernaturals out of hand, but their actions boiled down to bigotry through ignorance ending in murder. Some humans caused terrible pain for others without supernatural powers, while others gained supernatural powers and used them for good. Humans aren't good or bad and supernaturals aren't good or bad. Sapient beings can make a choice to live as they desire and giving up abilities that allow you to not only protect yourself, but others, from the horrors of the world (of darkness) shouldn't be an easy first choice.<br /> <br /> The problem for us was that it's the only clear choice presented by the books. Thus, we made a new path for our story. We first observed that the Qashmallim could effect the Disquiet and Wasteland produced by the Promethean. If they could do this fairly easily, why couldn't we eventually learn to do it? That would become the seed for us to develop a way. The end game would be acquiring the answer from an Arch Qashmallim, either through force or by convincing them that there was as much value in our path as that which most Promethean took. It assumes a lot about the Qashmallim and their own endgame that others might not like, but it worked well for us. While others may like the &quot;human end goal&quot; path, this ended up being a really enjoyable experience for us. Several of our group considered it to be one of their favorite campaigns to date, which is why I was excitedly checking the progress on the 2ed version. <br /> <br /> <br /> So, TL;DR version to help discussion: <br /> <br /> I was basically wondering how people feel about the idea that there are multiple &quot;right&quot; endgame goals for games like Promethean. It seems like a lot of people tend to take a strong right/wrong approach to the games where the purpose primarily stated in the books must be taken as golden. This results in either some refusing to buy the books if that bottom line disagrees with their view, or the other side telling those with complaints that they're wrong if they don't like it and should just find another game. <br /> <br /> Personally, I would like if there were more alternative paths, but I also understand that there's a word-count limit and the path they choose to focus on won't always be the one I would prefer, personally. In these cases, I've never hestitated to just go in another direction and slap together new rules to make it happen my way, if that's needed. Is that not something most people are cool with? Have many others changed things to better fit their ideal narrative, or do you always just work with what you're given or pass entirely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6191-the-lotus-eater","name":"The Lotus Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T17:02:06-07:00","id":532581,"title":"","content":"I have zero qualms with ignoring existing fluff and rules if it engages the players and makes for a good story. I could definitely see a refinement specifically based around surpassing the Promethean <i>and</i> Human state, especially seeing as the alchemy around which a lot of Promethean is based was supposed to be about perfecting humans in the first place.<br /> <br /> The fact that we're getting mortal alchemists in 2E should probably help flesh out transhuman ideas in Promethean, I think.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I also felt I should add, I was really drawn to Promethean for the same reasons I was drawn to Frankenstein. As a guy on the autistic spectrum, I could always relate to the Created, and I always felt that some of the Promethean state was (or could be interpreted as) sort of a metaphor for autism and other disorders. The thing about Promethean that I liked though, was that there was always hope. The Promethean could eventually learn to fit in with the world, and find a place where they could be loved and accepted. Hell, with the Athanors, they ended up having a slight edge over normal mortals. I don't think the idea behind the New Dawn is that you need to change yourself to fit in, so much as that fitting in is always going to be hard, but the rewards for toughing it out and finding a place in the world, whatever that might be, will be so worth it in the end. And even in the dark times, you don't have to be alone either. When you can't take the Torment, and everyone around you is stuck in Disquiet, you and your Throng can always rely on each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 05-29-2015, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T17:13:34-07:00","id":532593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean?p=532581#post532581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have zero qualms with ignoring existing fluff and rules if it engages the players and makes for a good story. I could definitely see a refinement specifically based around surpassing the Promethean <i>and</i> Human state, especially seeing as the alchemy around which a lot of Promethean is based was supposed to be about perfecting humans in the first place.<br /> <br /> The fact that we're getting mortal alchemists in 2E should probably help flesh out transhuman ideas in Promethean, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it would be interesting to see an official path for this, as well. I hope it wouldn't get sidelined as an antagonist specific path, like the Centimani, though. There should be the risk of megalomania taking hold and the hubris of those seeking to become &quot;greater&quot; being a corrupting force. I could definitely see where those seeking this would sometimes see mortals and other &quot;weaker&quot; beings as beneath them and seeing it as acceptable to treat them like annoying insects, or like livestock to be used for their own devices. I hope that wouldn't be the only focus, though. Something has to combat the malicious forces in the world of darkness. Some &quot;good&quot; beings have to be as powerful as the bad guys. I think there's plenty of non-malicious or negative reasons to want to preserve that kind of ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6191-the-lotus-eater","name":"The Lotus Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T17:27:11-07:00","id":532594,"title":"","content":"I couldn't get my friends interested in Promethean before. No one in my troupe wanted to play a splat based on not wanting to be that splat anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T18:05:41-07:00","id":532617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean?p=532594#post532594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I couldn't get my friends interested in Promethean before. No one in my troupe wanted to play a splat based on not wanting to be that splat anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Admittedly, Promethean is a hard sell. You could argue that Prometheans aren't trying to stop being Promethean, so much as start being Human. The difference is largely semantic, but I think the distinction is important. I'm sure that if they could, many Created would like to bring their powers with them through the New Dawn.<br /> <br /> On the topic of alternate paths, I had the briefest outlines of possible Refinements I could see:<ul><li><b>Chalybs (Steel):</b> Transcendence; Transcend Mortal and Promethean limitations</li> <li><b>Natrium (Sodium):</b> Syncretism; Incorporate aspects of other beings into yourself</li> <li><b>Orichalcum (Brass):</b> Friendship; I get by with a little help from my friends</li> <li><b>Carbonario (Coal):</b> Sacrifice; The New Dawn may only be reached through sacrifice</li> <li><b>Pyriten (Fool's Gold):</b> Qashmallim; Humanity is a red herring, the True Undertaking is to become a qashmal</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T18:33:52-07:00","id":532628,"title":"","content":"I think to me and my group, the drawbacks of the original goal aren't just that the Promethean has to give up their powers. That's sort of a similar state that Mummy ends in, with the freedom from the Judges (Apotheosis) requiring you sacrifice most of the supernatural benefits of being an Arisen. I don't know if that got as much friction as the Promethean issue, but at least it was never a problem for my group. The difference with Promethean is that it's not just about giving up supernatural abilities. It's about giving up your memories and the entirety of your being to become something entirely different than you are. The idea that you have to let go of power and ambition to reach a state of enlightenment is one thing. It's something that I think transhumanist enthusiasts would not like and I do think it's something that has good arguments on both sides. I wouldn't mind playing it, but I wouldn't mind playing paths that offer an alternative, either. That's not really the whole sacrifice of Promethean, though. The narrative basically asserts that Prometheans were created as something inherently wrong and that they won't be &quot;right&quot; until they give up everything (or at least very nearly everything) that they are in favor of becoming someone and something else entirely. I think that's a lot harder for some people to come to terms with than just sacrificing power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6191-the-lotus-eater","name":"The Lotus Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T18:36:58-07:00","id":532629,"title":"","content":"I can understand that. Personally, I ignore the memory loss part of the New Dawn except when it would serve the plot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T18:38:43-07:00","id":532631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean?p=532617#post532617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Admittedly, Promethean is a hard sell. You could argue that Prometheans aren't trying to stop being Promethean, so much as start being Human. The difference is largely semantic, but I think the distinction is important. I'm sure that if they could, many Created would like to bring their powers with them through the New Dawn.<br /> <br /> On the topic of alternate paths, I had the briefest outlines of possible Refinements I could see:<ul><li><b>Chalybs (Steel):</b> Transcendence; Transcend Mortal and Promethean limitations</li> <li><b>Natrium (Sodium):</b> Syncretism; Incorporate aspects of other beings into yourself</li> <li><b>Orichalcum (Brass):</b> Friendship; I get by with a little help from my friends</li> <li><b>Carbonario (Coal):</b> Sacrifice; The New Dawn may only be reached through sacrifice</li> <li><b>Pyriten (Fool's Gold):</b> Qashmallim; Humanity is a red herring, the True Undertaking is to become a qashmal</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking Platinum might make a good metaphor for Transhumanism: Rarer, more precious, and more &quot;incorruptible&quot; than Gold. Watching Big Hero 6 as I type this, BTW; great example of an artificial being exhibiting traits associated with the best of what &quot;Humanity&quot; has to offer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T23:52:27-07:00","id":532963,"title":"","content":"Yeah the whole giving up your past memories was something I always found problematic. Especially given that some former prometheans can even become antagonists. At the very least I believe any Promethean should be able to remember the lessons he learned on the pilgrimage if not their memories wholesale.<br /> <br /> If it helps think of the pilgrimage less of curing what makes you different, but owning and accepting it. Others hate the Promethean because they sense that they hate themselves, making the new dawn as much an acceptance of one's self as a human being as a physical transformation into one. From that standpoint, Centimanti are less about accepting one's current state, but rather reveling in one's self-loathing by truly acting as the monster one sees oneself as.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5823-ravian3","name":"Ravian3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T00:08:08-07:00","id":532964,"title":"","content":"Personally, I recast the amnesia as the final obstacle that you must push through to truly achieve your goal. That is, you've <i>physically</i> become human; but you're not <i>truly</i> finished until your memories return. <br /> <br /> There's a dissonance between the fluff and the rules on this: according to the fluff, most of the Redeemed end up as amnesiacs; according to the mechanics, if your Final Azoth Roll starts at two dice, you've got even odds of getting your memories back; more than that, and it becomes increasingly certain that you <i>will</i> get your memories back \u2014 it's just a matter of how long it will take. So as I said above, I recast it in terms of how long will it take to get your memories back, rather than <i>will</i> you get them back. In fact, I house-rule the Final Azoth Roll into an Extended Action, with the goal being to accumulate enough successes to retrieve your memory \u2014 and in the meantime, any Exceptional Successes you roll gives you some sort of reward, such as immunity to Disquiet or some sort of Boost. You remain human; but the better you do, the closer you are to being the best that humanity has to offer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T00:15:50-07:00","id":532969,"title":"","content":"I feel it's worth pointing out that the Refinement focused on Mortality is also the one with the most established capacity for memory alteration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T05:26:00-07:00","id":533045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Lotus Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean?p=532628#post532628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The narrative basically asserts that Prometheans were created as something inherently wrong and that they won't be &quot;right&quot; until they give up everything (or at least very nearly everything) that they are in favor of becoming someone and something else entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prometheans as they're made don't really <i>have</i> a being. They're mismatched bits of identity being constantly burned by the fire that rages in the gaps between them - the Pilgrimmage isn't about giving that up, it's about claiming a complete identity. Every step of the way, the whole world tells you you're an incomplete thing (and with the Wasteland, it really is the whole world telling you that) who could never be a person - but you answer that yes you can, and you tease out the kind of person you want to be, or that you already are, from the fragments inside you, from the relationships you forge in spite of everything - until you claim and understand that identity so profoundly that not even the world can deny it any more.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T07:15:10-07:00","id":533160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean?p=533045#post533045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prometheans as they're made don't really <i>have</i> a being. They're mismatched bits of identity being constantly burned by the fire that rages in the gaps between them - the Pilgrimmage isn't about giving that up, it's about claiming a complete identity. Every step of the way, the whole world tells you you're an incomplete thing (and with the Wasteland, it really is the whole world telling you that) who could never be a person - but you answer that yes you can, and you tease out the kind of person you want to be, or that you already are, from the fragments inside you, from the relationships you forge in spite of everything - until you claim and understand that identity so profoundly that not even the world can deny it any more.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I respect your interpretation, but I don't really find that a sapient creature like Prometheans can truly be lacking in identity. They're reasoning, thinking beings with a wide range of individualized emotions and that is, by my definition, an identity in itself. The Promethean has already built a pretty complex set of beliefs and ideals by the end of their Pilgrimage. I feel that way more reasoning and self-searching is required of them to even approach near the end of the Pilgrimage than most humans probably do in their whole life, but it's not questioned whether the human developed an identity. It can be said that Promethean don't have a &quot;true&quot; identity, but that's not what's represented to me by their experiences by the philosophical terms I personally subscribe to when defining the terms of an &quot;identity&quot;. I think identity is just the memories and experiences of a sapient being. They have that and they lose most of it by becoming human. I'm not saying that I don't think you're entitled to enjoy the narrative in the way you've presented it, but it's not for me, so I'm going to take another path. We're dealing with subjective philosophical concepts here, so it makes sense that people will verge on their interpretations of the material. Promethean are essentially whatever we say they are in the context of our own games, anyway. All that matters is that each group enjoys the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6191-the-lotus-eater","name":"The Lotus Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T13:37:34-07:00","id":533586,"title":"","content":"Prometheans are unstable things, in constant flux. The Pilgrimage is about achieving stability so that they can become a person, not a half-formed thing always a step away from dissolution. It isn't about humans being good or bad or supernatural things being good or bad. Ethics isn't the issue. Humanity is a huge spectrum of behavior and truths. You aren't giving up a unique identity to conform to some standard. Humanity has no standard. They are diverse and unique. Becoming human lets you become one of these diverse and unique individuals, too. What you are escaping is a half-life where the forces animating you compel you to change, to evolve or devolve, until you achieve stability or are destroyed. As I stated in another thread, Prometheans are on fire. You can't come to terms with being on fire and move on with your life. You either put the fire out or burn alive. Sacrificing your Promethean existence to be human is like a cancer patient abandoning that truth in order to be a healthy person. Very few would mourn losing their identity of &quot;terminal cancer patient&quot; in favor of the freedom to create a life around an identity they can choose and that won't destroy them.<br /> <br /> Short version: The Pilgrimage is about striving to not be broken. Unless you believe that sexual identity is a matter of being broken, there's no analogy to draw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T15:05:00-07:00","id":533665,"title":"","content":"<i>The Parable of the Lost Man</i><br /> <br /> One day, a man awoke in a house of mirrors; his reflection surrounded him, and he was hungry. &quot;Where am I?&quot; he cried, and the mirrors said &quot;In a place; you cannot leave until it is finished.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;How will it be finished?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Tell us where you are, and it will be complete.&quot;<br /> <br /> So the man searched for hours and hours through the hallways, his distorted reflections trailing off to infinity. After a seeming eternity, the mirrors spoke:<br /> <br /> &quot;Where are you?&quot;<br /> <br /> And the man answered<br /> <br /> &quot;I am right here.&quot;<br /> <br /> And he was no longer lost.<br /> <hr /><br /> To clarify:<br /> <br /> For Prometheans, the exit sign leads in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 05-30-2015, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T08:05:57-07:00","id":534323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Lotus Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean#post532418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never actually saw the complaint my group had with the Pilgrimage as one of a preference for transhumanism. To me, transhumanistic themes are more in-line with some Mage, Hunter and general God-Machine aspects. There are Legacies in the Mage material that certainly address transhumanism and, personally, I've always approached the Free Council as having a strong transhumanist slant among their majority. Some of the Hunter groups, like the Cheiron Group, Utopia Now or The Knights of Adrian certainly have strong transhumanist elements, but I feel like Hunter is especially thick with this philosophy. When it comes to Promethean, I would have only really even thought &quot;transhumanism&quot; when it came to certain technologically heavy backgrounds for the Unfleshed. Even then, though, the person created isn't and was never human.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are here swaping <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transhumanism\" target=\"_blank\">transhumanism</a> with <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Technophilia\" target=\"_blank\">technophilia</a>. Transhumanism is about supressing limits of human condition. Technophilia is about being dedicated to engaging and developmment of technology.<br /> <br /> Whole <b>Mage</b>, in nutshell, is all about transhumanism, in it's background. You play humans that were grants powers of gods and can become immortal, move mountains and read the future. <i>Any</i> Order in game is supporting this. Only Free Council have strong technophilia elements, like Sleepers transhmanists movements now, becuase both groups belives that by the technology, they can become transhuman beings. Rest of Orders thinks they can become transhumans only by the ancient spells. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Lotus Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean#post532418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that they weren't human and, yet, their only acceptable goal is to become so is what was unappealing to my group. Of course there are drawbacks of being a Promethean, extreme ones. The Wasteland is the one that can't really be ignored simply by removing themselves from human society, but a big focus on what's &quot;wrong&quot; with being a Promethean is that humans react negatively to them. The general feelings of my group were probably colored largely by the fact that we're all somewhere on the LGBT spectrum and some have alternative gender identities they've struggled with, as well as some of those same people experiencing the double edged bigotry sword of added racism, so a couple of our group members couldn't get past the idea that becoming human was just giving up what made the Promethean who they were in order to gain acceptance from their tormenters. There was no way they could get comfortable with the idea of a character that would sacrifice their inherent individuality (as the players saw it, at least) in order to appeal to the majority expectations. It would always come back as a reflection of the question in their mind, &quot;If there was a way to undo the thing people persecute ME for, should I take that choice?&quot;. A game that in any way implied they should caused them discomfort and ruined their interest.</div> </div> </div> </div>As <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear_(gay_culture)\" target=\"_blank\">bisexual bear </a>in very homophobic country, I can <u>totally</u> understand those feelings. And it's aso one of the reasons why I'm interested aboud <b>Promethean</b> - beside alchemy and Franeknsteain monsters. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Lotus Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean#post532418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, we could recognize that this wasn't really the intended message. The Prometheans aren't facing homophobia or racism, even if the rejection they experience can pick at the insecurities of players that have experienced those things. We didn't feel the need to shun the material, because it actually had a lot of aspects that really hit home with us. The journey of these beings to overcome the external torments inflicted on them and find peace inside themselves was actually extremely appealing to us without the suggested endgame goal. Our alternative was that the endgame goal wouldn't be to become human, but to find a way to control the Divine Fire inside ourselves so that our characters wouldn't have to give up what they were, their memories, etc, and could continue on with their lives gaining acceptance for what they were and not only by sacrificing themselves to become something new.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the &quot;Alternative Goal&quot; I discuessed many times with creators. I assume some ( not all, or even majority ) of Created would want to be left the being they are, only more stable, with harnessed Divine Fire. It's a stance i fight on this forum to be included, even only in small frame in 2ED corebook. Because there are rather large portion of Promethean <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Lotus Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean#post532418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We focused our character Refinements on Mercurius, Stannum, Argentum, Cobalus and Plumbum. We made it a focus to study Pyros, but also the existence of other supernatural creatures, but not to see how it was lesser or more flawed than the existence of humans. We found an interesting theme to explore in our game was how supernatural entities and mortal humans were truly no better or worse than each other. &quot;Humanity&quot; wasn't just for humans. A werewolf, or vampire or even more &quot;non-human&quot; creatures could be kind, helpful beings that used their power to help others. We, as Promethean, could do that. Some mortal human Hunter archetypes claim to be doing good by slaughtering supernaturals out of hand, but their actions boiled down to bigotry through ignorance ending in murder. Some humans caused terrible pain for others without supernatural powers, while others gained supernatural powers and used them for good. Humans aren't good or bad and supernaturals aren't good or bad. Sapient beings can make a choice to live as they desire and giving up abilities that allow you to not only protect yourself, but others, from the horrors of the world (of darkness) shouldn't be an easy first choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good choicses, here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Most of us - &quot;transhuman&quot; <b>Promethean</b> fans - was think about the same collection and mostly the same reasons. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Lotus Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean#post532418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I would like if there were more alternative paths, but I also understand that there's a word-count limit and the path they choose to focus on won't always be the one I would prefer, personally. In these cases, I've never hestitated to just go in another direction and slap together new rules to make it happen my way, if that's needed. Is that not something most people are cool with? Have many others changed things to better fit their ideal narrative, or do you always just work with what you're given or pass entirely?</div> </div> </div> </div>Beside the Refiments shift that are made in 2ED <b>required</b>? I think one frame of text that only highlights general motive - those of Created that want to be &quot;transhuman&quot;, just do not want to end Pilgirmage, rather find a way for stable existance. It's just a few little tweaks needed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T19:55:12-08:00","id":836820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean?p=533586#post533586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prometheans are unstable things, in constant flux. The Pilgrimage is about achieving stability so that they can become a person, not a half-formed thing always a step away from dissolution. It isn't about humans being good or bad or supernatural things being good or bad. Ethics isn't the issue. Humanity is a huge spectrum of behavior and truths. You aren't giving up a unique identity to conform to some standard. Humanity has no standard. They are diverse and unique. Becoming human lets you become one of these diverse and unique individuals, too. What you are escaping is a half-life where the forces animating you compel you to change, to evolve or devolve, until you achieve stability or are destroyed. As I stated in another thread, Prometheans are on fire. You can't come to terms with being on fire and move on with your life. You either put the fire out or burn alive. Sacrificing your Promethean existence to be human is like a cancer patient abandoning that truth in order to be a healthy person. Very few would mourn losing their identity of &amp;quot;terminal cancer patient&amp;quot; in favor of the freedom to create a life around an identity they can choose and that won't destroy them.<br /> <br /> Short version: The Pilgrimage is about striving to not be broken. Unless you believe that sexual identity is a matter of being broken, there's no analogy to draw.</div> </div> </div> </div>My dude, there's a world of difference between having cancer and being an immortal robot that the universe hates for no good reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T20:14:37-08:00","id":836827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean?p=836820#post836820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My dude, there's a world of difference between having cancer and being an immortal robot that the universe hates for no good reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>You and I have very different standards of immortality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T23:29:02-08:00","id":836876,"title":"","content":"Not the least of which is that Prometheans demonstably are not immortal. Obscenely long lived, sure, but not immortal.<br /> <br /> Also, the universe 'hates you' because you are a constant, unmitigated source of perpetual change on every level, and without direction, that manifests as entropy, in self, in others, in nature.<br /> <br /> These things don't just happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-25-2016, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T23:37:12-08:00","id":836878,"title":"","content":"As a LGBT person myself, I do not feel comfortable with the comparison between my sexual preferences, which are harmless, and a Promethean's condition, which is objectively harmful on both a physical and a psychological level, for everyone around them. People do not hate Prometheans because they're bigoted, they hate Prometheans because the Azoth poisons their minds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T23:48:01-08:00","id":836883,"title":"","content":"That's because Prometheans are not a metaphor for specific groups of society. It's an exaggeration on the entire human experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T05:24:41-08:00","id":836982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean?p=836878#post836878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a LGBT person myself, I do not feel comfortable with the comparison between my sexual preferences, which are harmless, and a Promethean's condition, which is objectively harmful on both a physical and a psychological level, for everyone around them. People do not hate Prometheans because they're bigoted, they hate Prometheans because the Azoth poisons their minds.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny when people compare the Promethean existence to LGBT.<br /> <br /> -Prometheans are <i>Created</i>, Right there in the title.<br /> -Prometheans are <i>Monsters</i><br /> -Prometheans are different. So different that nature itself is repulsed.<br /> -Prometheans are on a quest to stop their constant changes.<br /> <br /> But then we get into the LGBT, people who are:<br /> <br /> -Born that way.<br /> -100% human<br /> -Different on such a superficial level that it's ridiculous. And bigots hate them for reasons lost to all.<br /> -Probably not on a quest to do anything else than their little life<br /> <br /> Promethean is not a game about a trans-person learning how to shut the fuck up and be a real man/woman. It's not the story of a lesbian finally understanding that she should live with a boy if she wants to have children. It's a game about finding your place in the world, and the symbolism used to achieve that is humanity and the Pilgrimage.<br /> <br /> If you really want to make Promethean about LGBT people, fine, but stop thinking that the metaphor is that Prometheans are unique snowflakes trying to become like everyone else, and see that it's a quest to find your place, your calling, your loves, etc... Because when a Promethean achieves her New Dawn, she can be whatever she wants to. A Trigendered Bisexual handicapped Female? Sure. An old, boring businessman? Just as easy. You can become whoever you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T07:22:58-08:00","id":837017,"title":"","content":"I think ShadowKnight1224 was expressing discomfort with that comparison, not making it themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T07:26:40-08:00","id":837019,"title":"","content":"Oh. Hm. Well, sorry about that ShadowKnight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T07:39:44-08:00","id":837024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean?p=837019#post837019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh. Hm. Well, sorry about that ShadowKnight.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries! I appreciate your post anyway, as it goes into detail about what I found uncomfortable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T09:20:43-08:00","id":837054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Lotus Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean#post532418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, TL;DR version to help discussion:<br /> <br /> I was basically wondering how people feel about the idea that there are multiple &quot;right&quot; endgame goals for games like Promethean. It seems like a lot of people tend to take a strong right/wrong approach to the games where the purpose primarily stated in the books must be taken as golden. This results in either some refusing to buy the books if that bottom line disagrees with their view, or the other side telling those with complaints that they're wrong if they don't like it and should just find another game.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would like if there were more alternative paths, but I also understand that there's a word-count limit and the path they choose to focus on won't always be the one I would prefer, personally. In these cases, I've never hestitated to just go in another direction and slap together new rules to make it happen my way, if that's needed. Is that not something most people are cool with? Have many others changed things to better fit their ideal narrative, or do you always just work with what you're given or pass entirely?</div> </div> </div> </div> I never really pushed the whole &quot;becoming human&quot; thing. I always focused on the &quot;stop being a monster&quot; part, and let the story go from there. To me, Promethean isn't so much of a game about fitting in - that's Aurum alone, as far as I'm concerned. Each Refinement has its own path towards the New Dawn: <br /> <br /> Aurum, the Refinement of Gold, does focus on fitting in to human society. They're called Mimics for a reason. The other four core Refinements? Don't really care about &quot;fitting in.&quot; Tin, the Refinement of Torment, is all about understanding your anger and fears, the dark little impulses in your mind, and coming to terms with them. Copper is more about the wise man of the wilderness. They're people who go out and find balance with the natural world and those that go with them - screw everyone else. Mercurius took a more scientific / medical perspective of what being a monster was, and how to balance your body chemistry. Iron is all about perfect control over the spirit by mastering the body.<br /> <br /> I don't see any reason we need to focus on &quot;fitting in&quot; when that's only one of the many paths. &quot;Becoming human&quot; can mean almost anything. To use your group as an example, the New Dawn isn't taking someone on the LGTB spectrum and forcing them to conform (unless they want to). Its about taking all the anger and rage and inner torment over the people's rejection and turning it into something positive. Its about building a life that doesn't involve those ugly emotions. Because Promtheans aren't people with a healthy drives. They're broken people with lots of emotional and psychological baggage that they need to work through. They have serious issues that need to be addresed. <br /> <br /> Anways, I have no problems with Prometheans after achieving the New Dawn to still have access to their same spiritual alchemies. Or &quot;becoming more than human.&quot; Because Promethean has just as much resonance with a mage's Ascension as it does with a vampire's Golconda path. The thing that sticks in my craw at this point is that most people just carry a very narrow definition of human into the game. Especially in the CofD, where humans are innately magical and have so much potential. And I'm not just talking about mages; I'm talking about mundane people as well. Despite all the monsters, the CofD has some very bright potential that reality doesn't match up to either. The silver linings are pretty brilliant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T11:30:57-08:00","id":837114,"title":"","content":"It's really simple, actually: Prometheans can't stay the way they are because Qashmallim are a bunch of total dicks who have made it the purpose of their very existence to endlessly troll Prometheans until they aren't Prometheans anymore. It's not actually about becoming human -- that the Prometheans are no longer trolled once they become human is simply a side-effect of the fact that humans aren't as fun to troll as Prometheans are -- it's because Qashmallim are easily amused, and despite apparently being super important embodiments of some important principle or another, they literally have nothing better to do than to make Prometheans miserable for their own amusement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":8950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","user":"Vithrir","date":". 02-25-2016, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T11:52:56-08:00","id":837131,"title":"","content":"You can have an entire Promethean chronicle without a Qashmal, and still stay true to the core theme. Might even be better off. Their interference has little to do with why a Promethean sojourns, let alone towards humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T12:22:48-08:00","id":837149,"title":"","content":"I very much got the impression in 1E that the qashmallim were not expected to be regular chronicle features.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T12:29:31-08:00","id":837154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean?p=837149#post837149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I very much got the impression in 1E that the qashmallim were not expected to be regular chronicle features.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on what I'd seen of the 2E preview, qashmallim will literally intervene to make a Promethean's life miserable, possibly invoking wastelands and/or firestorms, if they aren't pursuing the New Dawn.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T12:39:06-08:00","id":837163,"title":"","content":"Wastelands really do suck, but as I understand it the only qashmallim that will provoke Wastelands are the powerful ones, Rank 3+ (if qashmallim are using Rank now). It could just be the unfortunate side effect of a sufficient powerful messenger from the Principle. As to Firestorms, they aren't necessarily a <i>bad </i>thing. One of the impressions I got from the spoilers is that Firestorms are sort of like any other natural disaster, apart from the whole 'born from the Divine Fire' thing, in that they occur when tensions in different forces grow too high. Wastelands start to build to intolerable levels? Boom- Firestorm. The release of Pyros ends the Wasteland and allows things to get back to normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T12:40:48-08:00","id":837165,"title":"","content":"#NotEveryPilgramage<br /> <br /> The qashmallim and Principle are the 'black box mysteries' of Promethean, an area where weirdness prevails, in much the same way that hob/goblins in Changeling is this big ol' bag of weirdness. Each game has their known places and quantities, and then they have the &quot;there be dragons&quot; area.<br /> <br /> The qashmallim and Principle are tied to the forces at work in the Pilgramage-they have to be, because Promethean is a tight, thematically focused game. But the reasons why this sea of divine fire and it's occasionally acting drops of change get involved are not the end-all, be-all of the pilgramage. It's entirely possible something else is going on that just happens to be related to Prometheans chasing the New Dawn.<br /> <br /> My point, more or less, is that I don't think the way it was presented in the blog means that Qashmallim are more of a thing. They are clarified, put to purpose, but that purpose and the effects of their missions are strange and alien, made worse because they have this central uniting feature that might not actually be central at all. Qashmallim exist to cast shadows on the otherwise 'simple' world of the Pilgramage, to raise questions without answers, doubts without satiation, and fear from your characters hopes.<br /> <br /> Here, there be angels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T13:32:30-08:00","id":837190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean?p=837149#post837149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I very much got the impression in 1E that the qashmallim were not expected to be regular chronicle features.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Huh. I used them all the time.<br /> <br /> But then, hobgoblins are regular features in my Changeling games as well. I guess that's just my play/running style. Considering that I use the strix with fair frequency, as well as the Abyss and Scelesti along with Reapers, I'm pretty well into the black box coming standard, it seems.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-25-2016, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T13:56:56-08:00","id":837205,"title":"","content":"I used hobgoblins a lot too, that's not quite my point. My point with the hobgoblins and the entire goblin thing is, well....not to be derogatory, I just need to say it like this, but have you seen hobgoblins?<br /> <br /> Of course you have, but what I mean by that is that in the general sense of changelings' narrative, hobgoblins don't fit nicely. You can't classify them the way you can Huntsmen, Strangers, and changelings, the whole motley bunch defy sense and sanity in any categorical way. I can generally place them as a primarily Going Home problem as well as a way to round out Leaving Arcadia problems, but beyond that, they are wild, unruly, and create this big space of weirdness where Changeling kind of challenges Changeling. It's all strangeness and murk with all things goblins.<br /> <br /> Coming back to Promethean, the qashmallim fit the same sort of box. Everything else fits into the box of Promethean's narrative 'neatly', but the qashmallim come in muddle the entire thing-the flow is broken by their presence and interference. Hell, as much as they egg on the pilgramage, their presence is one of the biggest factors to make a Promethean question whether or not chasing the New Dawn is a good thing for them or not. Before, it was a personal escap,e now it serves a purpose you're not privy too, if nothing else, and that's ignoring the nature of what they do with or to Prometheans on the individual basis.<br /> <br /> The difference between the hob/goblin and the qashmallim is that the weirdness has more place in the common Changeling game than it does in the Promethean game. Hob/goblin(s) just don't upset the apple cart in the same way the qashmallim do. I will always find a reason to slip that into changeling. I might go an entire game of Promethean without ever having a qashmallim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T14:44:49-08:00","id":837225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean?p=837114#post837114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's really simple, actually: Prometheans can't stay the way they are because Qashmallim are a bunch of total dicks who have made it the purpose of their very existence to endlessly troll Prometheans until they aren't Prometheans anymore. It's not actually about becoming human -- that the Prometheans are no longer trolled once they become human is simply a side-effect of the fact that humans aren't as fun to troll as Prometheans are -- it's because Qashmallim are easily amused, and despite apparently being super important embodiments of some important principle or another, they literally have nothing better to do than to make Prometheans miserable for their own amusement.</div> </div> </div> </div>As others have pointed out, that ain't necessarily so. Sure, you <i>can</i> play it that way if you so choose; but by default, <i>qashmallim</i> simply aren't around that much. <br /> <br /> I also find it interesting that at least two posters have characterized the Promethean condition in terms of outside entities harassing the Woobie \u201cfor no good reason\u201d or \u201cbecause they're dicks\u201d, implying that there's nothing wrong with the Promethean condition itself. Forget about Torment, where the Humours that animate the Created surge out of control and drive it to destructive behaviors; forget about the fact that Wasteland is less about the land rejecting the Promethean and more about the Promethean's presence poisoning the land; and never mind that even Disquiet isn't so much about people fearing the Other as it is about Azothic radiation poisoning peoples' minds. <b>Promethean</b> isn't a game about misunderstood protagonists overcoming bigotry and coming to realize that they're fine as they are; it's a game about <i>flawed</i> protagonists coming to understand that they're flawed and <i>fixing</i> the flaws. <br /> <br /> And with that in mind, <i>qashmallim</i> typically don't guide and harass Prometheans out of spite or malice; they do so to remind the Promethean that it <i>is</i> flawed, and to motivate it to get back to the work of correcting its flaws. I think of it more like them being agents of an absentee parent (the Principle) who provide the tough love that the Promethean needs to eventually achieve its potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T17:40:21-08:00","id":837313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean?p=837205#post837205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the qashmallim come in muddle the entire thing-the flow is broken by their presence and interference. Hell, as much as they egg on the pilgramage, their presence is one of the biggest factors to make a Promethean question whether or not chasing the New Dawn is a good thing for them or not. Before, it was a personal escape now it serves a purpose you're not privy too, if nothing else, and that's ignoring the nature of what they do with or to Prometheans on the individual basis.<br /> <br /> The difference between the hob/goblin and the qashmallim is that the weirdness has more place in the common Changeling game than it does in the Promethean game. Hob/goblin(s) just don't upset the apple cart in the same way the qashmallim do. I will always find a reason to slip that into changeling. I might go an entire game of Promethean without ever having a qashmallim.</div> </div> </div> </div> Honestly? It sounds like you're describing the qashmallim like they're Firestorms.<br /> <br /> What do I mean by that? Each of the title creatures/phenomenon (strix, idigam, fallen world, firestorm, huntsmen, slashers, keroberus) are built to be the ones who are the status- quo shakers. They're the ones who upset the apple carts, throw the monkey wrench into the works, etc. When these happen, everything goes to hell in a handbasket.<br /> <br /> That seems to be the level of craziness you're attributing to the qashmallim. Now, if memory serves, there IS a tie between firestorms and quashmallim, but I can't remember exactly what it is. But I'm not entirely sure if &quot;upsetting the applecart&quot; is really the driving story principle behind these luminous beings. That seat has already been taken, and I don't know if wew really have two kinds of that driving. I don't know if you know something I don't (more than likely), but that feels kind of off to me, simply because of narrative overlap.<br /> <br /> The qashmallim, irregardless of choir, are agents of change. They're transformative - both in an enlightened sense, and a transformative sense. But change is actually the status quo for the alchemical Prometheans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-25-2016, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T17:59:54-08:00","id":837322,"title":"","content":"Firestorms, as I know it, are stage-setters for dramatic milestones. But I don't know them very well, I admit.<br /> <br /> I would have thought, ages ago, that the qashmallim should have been the subject of the chronicle name...if I thought I could make a case for any given game having to deal with them like I do the rest. I don't feel that compulsion though. The few times I have run Promethean, it never even occurred to me to use them. In every plan I have for future games in Promethean, I just don't think about the qashmallim. Truth be told, the qashmallim and the Principle kind of bore me. They are singularly the least interesting part of Promethean for me.<br /> <br /> But that said, am I wrong in saying the qashmallim are the single weirdest part of the entire game? I don't feel like I'm off base by saying that it's the biggest murky part of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T18:12:03-08:00","id":837330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean?p=837149#post837149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I very much got the impression in 1E that the qashmallim were not expected to be regular chronicle features.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, they're rare in the Firestorm Chronicle anthology, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T20:20:16-08:00","id":837375,"title":"","content":"I'm not really quite sure what you mean by single weirdest part of the game. I don't think they're any stranger than the goddesses Venus and Isis being founders of two Lineages of monsters. Promethean has always had an element of &quot;stealing the Fire of God.&quot; Both literally and figuratively here. So, its not a stretch to see godly beings in the game. At least, that's my opinion. I don't see them as murky- they're pretty clear cut to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T00:46:46-08:00","id":837427,"title":"","content":"I've always seen them as story catalysts, rather than a focal point. Their mystery isn't meant to be penetrable. They serve better as signposts than they do anything else, and their Deus Ex Machina role is best kept to the barest of minimums.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing though: they are bloody awesome. Beings made of fire and inspiration, with divinity their fuel and bringing messages and prophecies from on high. Just one is enough to ratchet up a chronicle from a sedate contemplation to a Revelations-style apocalypse as you see fit, and you don't even have to contrive some sort of context, like you might for an idigam to, say, take every first-born son or turn the seas to blood.<br /> <br /> That sort of power isn't the right tool for every job, but used wisely, they show just how monumental and incredible the Pilgrimage truly is. Prometheans were born out of attempts to play God, and the Principle seems to hold that just playing counts. The Qashmallim confirm in their attentions that the Prometheans have divine value and potential, and are capable of literal miracles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T06:57:04-08:00","id":842533,"title":"","content":"So a thread on a &quot;transhuman&quot; (the quote marks are deliberate for reasons I'm about to elaborate on) hack just got closed, but what it did do was crystalise my thoughts on why none of these attempts have worked for me. Which is that they never actually evoke transhumanism, just a hatred of humanity.<br /> <br /> Ever heard the line, &quot;Don't knock stone age medicine; it's the reason we survived long enough to have a bronze age?&quot;<br /> <br /> It's been observed by various posters that you have be human before you can be transhuman, but mostly in the context of defending the Pilgrimmage as is. But it applies another way, that to be transhuman, it has to be something <i>humans can achieve.</i> None of the so called transhuman hacks for Promethean incorporate that - they're all ways for Prometheans to become things that are more powerful than humans, or lose all their weaknesses while keeping all their powers. In other words, just ways for the powerful to become more powerful.<br /> <br /> In the real world, if transhumanity ever comes to be, it'll be because of humanity, just like with the aforementioned medicine. So it's not enough to base a transhuman hack on &quot;humans suck&quot; - it has to be something human will and endeavour can attain - and that's something that fits way better with the humanism of Promethean.<br /> <br /> So here's a rough go at one that <i>does</i> that, which I'm going to call a Heraklean:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 03-05-2016, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T06:58:43-08:00","id":842535,"title":"","content":"BASELINE:<br /> <br /> A Heraklean is a human who has awakened a seed of Azoth inside them. For the moment, this is an Azoth of 0 - it exists, but it doesn't do a whole lot. Its radiance only extends to the same room, and the Heraklean cannot store Pyros inside her body - instead, she must use an external Alembic (we can assume a PC has made one of these). [I've not thought about how to render an Alembic mechanically beyond this yet]<br /> <br /> Pyros can be gathered through the same means as for a Promethean, though it's the Alembic that must be in the right place at the right time.<br /> <br /> Herakleans have Humours and Hopes. Humour works like vice, and if the Heraklean starts picking up Promethean weaknesses, characterises them the way Lineage does; it represents a major and unchanging aspect of the character's personality. Hope represents a framework for the character's aspirations, and what drives her to exceed her humanity; mechanically, it works like virtue. [Humours can be anything that would make sense for an alchemical or quasi-alchemical Humour; Hopes, I guess, would be similar to virtues and vices?]<br /> <br /> Herakleans still have Integrity.<br /> <br /> They can form Alchemical Pacts, though at this stage, there's little point.<br /> <br /> <br /> REFINEMENTS:<br /> <br /> These are the eight of the same ten as the Promethean ones, though they have different emphases, because the character has to learn different things. [Really, they should have a different name than Refinement]<br /> <br /> Each Refinement is the study of self and/or world. Aurum is of ties to humanity, Cuprum of your own mind and dreams, Ferrum of your body, Mercurius of the Fire you hope to draw further into yourself, Stannum of your impulses and instincts, Aes of your ties to other seekers on this path, Argentum of the supernatural world, Cobalus of recognising your imperfections, Phosphorum of the nature of change, and Plumbum of the physical world. [Plumbum is deliberately different: &quot;the human condition&quot; is covered by the others, and there ought to be a Refinement for the physical world; maybe it should also have a different name] [Also, I'm decidedly not happy with Phosphorum]<br /> <br /> Unlike Prometheans, A Heraklean's Refinements have dot values, 1-10: these are the equivalents of Pilgrimmage levels (yes, a Heraklean is on ten pilgrimmages at once, potentially - no one said this would be easy).<br /> <br /> Rather than a cost-break on Transmutations, a Heraklean can only learn those of the Refinements she has dots in.<br /> <br /> Milestones show up along the way, and provide Vitriol as normal. These can be used to buy dots in whichever Refinements are appropriate to the lesson learned in the milestone. [This is based on first edition milestones, which seem more appropriate for Herakleans than second edition ones]<br /> <br /> <br /> WEDDINGS:<br /> <br /> The baseline aspects of the Promethean condition are paired up, one strength and one weakness. My current thinking here is:<br /> <br /> Azoth goes to 1, and can increase further, allowing the Heraklean to hold Pyros inside + Wasteland. [These are the apices - is the plural of apex apices or apexes? - of the inner Fire]<br /> <br /> Transhuman potential (ie attribute buffing) + Torment. [Both represent your energy surging out of you and pushing you]<br /> <br /> Healed by electricity + Hurt by fire. [Conductivity for good or ill]<br /> <br /> Superlative Endurance/Constitution (and adding immortality) + Pandorans wanna eat ya! [As your body's substance is perfected, it becomes appetising to those who long for Azoth]<br /> <br /> Ability to perform a Generative Act + Disquiet. [Your inner Fire wants to spread to other kindling, and wears on the psyches of those around you]<br /> <br /> Each of these pairs is also associated with a pair of Refinements [though I haven't formulated thoughts on that yet]. When you feel sufficiently advanced in one of these (you don't get to add them), you can attempt a Wedding roll, similar to a New Dawn roll: on an exceptional success you get the benefit without the weakness, on a regular success you get both, on a failure you get nothing, and on a dramatic failure you get only the weakness; however it turns out, you lose all dots in that Refinement (though you can start again if you want).<br /> <br /> <br /> PROMETHEANS:<br /> <br /> Prometheans can do this as well, but they must finish a regular Pilgrimmage first: to transcend humanity, you must first attain it. When a Promethean reaches the New Dawn, rather than becoming human, she can choose to remain as she is and seek the Heraklean Weddings. This means revisiting the Refinements in light of her new insight and condition, but some of the work is done (she can distribute her old Pilgrimmage dots among any Refinements she spent time on).<br /> <br /> A Promethean on this path replaces Pilgrimmage with Integrity. Unlike a Heraklean, she can learn any sort of Transmutation, though - being less volatile - she no longer gets cost breaks. She also gets a Humour and Hope.<br /> <br /> When she's ready for a Wedding, an exceptional success eliminates the paired weakness, while a regular success or failure has no effect. A dramatic failure doesn't eliminate any of her power however - it destroys her hard-won soul, reinstating all Promethean weaknesses and returning her to the beginning of her Pilgrimmage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ADDENDUM 1; LESS BOOKKEEPING:<br /> <br /> Rather than tracking dots for all ten Refinements, you're on one and one only until you roll for your Wedding or abandon it for another (losing all your progress either way). In this case, I would link your Hope with one Refinement, in which you would keep your dots even if you spend time on another path.<br /> <br /> <br /> ADDENDUM 2; 8/10:<br /> <br /> As I said, I'm not too happy with my idea for Phosphorum. And Argentum seems less relevant here than it does for Prometheans. So maybe drop those two, and Herakleans only have eight. In this case, Ability to perform a Generative Act and Pandorans wanna eat ya! would go into the baseline, while Superlative Endurance/Constitution would now be paired with Disquiet (your body no longer perfoms quite the same give and take with the world - the absence can imbalance the psyches of people near you).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T08:17:10-08:00","id":842572,"title":"","content":"I'm waiting to see what 2e does with alchemists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T16:00:48-08:00","id":842757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean?p=842535#post842535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> 