klean, she can learn any sort of Transmutation, though - being less volatile - she no longer gets cost breaks. She also gets a Humour and Hope.<br /> <br /> When she's ready for a Wedding, an exceptional success eliminates the paired weakness, while a regular success or failure has no effect. A dramatic failure doesn't eliminate any of her power however - it destroys her hard-won soul, reinstating all Promethean weaknesses and returning her to the beginning of her Pilgrimmage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ADDENDUM 1; LESS BOOKKEEPING:<br /> <br /> Rather than tracking dots for all ten Refinements, you're on one and one only until you roll for your Wedding or abandon it for another (losing all your progress either way). In this case, I would link your Hope with one Refinement, in which you would keep your dots even if you spend time on another path.<br /> <br /> <br /> ADDENDUM 2; 8/10:<br /> <br /> As I said, I'm not too happy with my idea for Phosphorum. And Argentum seems less relevant here than it does for Prometheans. So maybe drop those two, and Herakleans only have eight. In this case, Ability to perform a Generative Act and Pandorans wanna eat ya! would go into the baseline, while Superlative Endurance/Constitution would now be paired with Disquiet (your body no longer perfoms quite the same give and take with the world - the absence can imbalance the psyches of people near you).</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>This could go hand-in-hand with my own idea for a post-New Dawn splat/alternate destination, found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage/page2\">here.</a> <br /> <br /> \u200bIf you are going with the name Herakleans, might I suggest you that you change Refinements to Labors, and that you will need MORE of them, not less?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T04:28:21-08:00","id":842948,"title":"","content":"Twelve Refinements/Labours would maybe imply three of them leading to each of four pairs of strengths/weaknesses. I guess one of the new ones should be Salt, don't know about the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T02:31:15-08:00","id":844985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean?p=842572#post842572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm waiting to see what 2e does with alchemists.</div> </div> </div> </div> One oft overlooked / ignored part of 1e Promethean? In the core book antagonist section? There is a guy who discovered how to make clones from a captured prommie. We basically have a Disquiet-addled human scientist tapping into the Azoth within the prommie to advance his perverted work. <br /> <br /> I bet almost anything that this is going to be an example of alchemist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T04:07:42-08:00","id":845003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean?p=842533#post842533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been observed by various posters that you have be human before you can be transhuman, but mostly in the context of defending the Pilgrimmage as is. But it applies another way, that to be transhuman, it has to be something <i>humans can achieve.</i></div> </div> </div> </div> You know, one thing that always boggled my mind in these conversations? Well, two things actually. <br /> <br /> The first is that humans have some very neat tricks they can pull off in the CofD. Immorality, psychic ability, cyborgnetic enhancements. Honestly, if I wanted to be an existance that was biologically and spiritually superior to the average human? Very doable as is. When the first book came out, I made a house rule that all New Dawns automatically got the equivalent of an Exceptional Success, remembring everything and Sleepwalker status and all that. I upped the benefits from Athanors, and suggested that they'd have automatic access to Second Sight thaumaturgy and psychic abilities. My players loved that idea. <br /> <br /> The second thing that boggles my mind is that people put so much emphasis on the New Dawn and what you become. The New Dawn is the end game. As in, the game is generally <i>over</i> at that point. When my players asked why I was so generous with post-New Dawn, I told them. Game's pretty much over, we're no longer playing Promethean at that point. I'm happy to start a new game using the new-humans in a new direction, which is why they'd get all that stuff. The group unanimously turned down that idea, they'd want new PCs. <br /> <br /> If someone comes up to me and wants to be better-than-human, what do I care? The game is over at that point, and I find that it has little to no impact on the game play itself. The only time I saw it have any impact at all was when someone ended up effectively wanting to do a Centimani-style character without actually being Centimani. Eventually, the character ended up going Flux anyways, and got abandoned by the other PCs when they found out he was on that path. <br /> <br /> I just.... don't understand why there's all this focus on being something after the New Dawn. The game is over. You've reached the finish line. Are you going to keep playing the same PC? Then the kind of game you play after should determine your abilities. If not? Why does it matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T05:54:23-08:00","id":845035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean?p=845003#post845003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just.... don't understand why there's all this focus on being something after the New Dawn. The game is over. You've reached the 